3:["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-4 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":["The common counter-argument - \"our audience is impatient, get to the button fast\" - confuses speed with sequence. You can keep the page short. The proof can be a single stat or one line from a client. What matters is that it appears ",["$","em",null,{"children":"before"}]," the ask, not that it takes three scrolls to find."]}]
4:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"What Actually Counts as Proof"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-5 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Not every social proof element carries equal weight. Generic testimonials (\"Amazing team!\") are nearly worthless. Proof earns trust in proportion to its specificity and verifiability. Useful proof formats to test include:"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-4 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Outcome statistics with context."}]," ","\"A documented before-and-after result tied to a specific intervention.\" The claim is useful only when the source, period, and method are inspectable."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Case study snippets."}]," ","A two-sentence before/after: the problem, the fix, the result. No narrative padding. Visitors can pattern-match their situation to the example in under ten seconds."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Named testimonials with role and company."}]," ","\"Sarah L., Performance Marketing Manager, [Company]\" gives the visitor more context than \"Sarah L.\" alone. The role signals that the reviewer has relevant authority to assess the claim."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Recognisable logos."}]," ","Client or publication logos work as borrowed credibility. One recognisable name does more work than a row of unknowns. Include logos only when the relationship is real and verifiable."]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The test for any proof element: can a visitor understand the claim and its relevance in under ten seconds? If not, compress it or cut it. Density beats volume."}]]}]
5:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Where to Place Proof Relative to the CTA"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-5 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"A useful experiment is to place one relevant proof element before the first meaningful CTA. \"Meaningful\" means any button asking for contact details, a purchase, a demo, or a free trial. Here are three sequence patterns to test:"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-fg-muted","children":"Minimal (short pages)"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-1 text-sm text-fg-muted","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"1."}]," Headline + subheadline"]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"2."}]," One outcome stat or logo strip"]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"3."}]," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-fg font-semibold","children":"CTA"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-fg-muted","children":"Standard (mid-length pages)"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-1 text-sm text-fg-muted","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"1."}]," Headline + subheadline"]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"2."}]," Problem statement"]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"3."}]," Named testimonial or case snippet"]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"4."}]," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-fg font-semibold","children":"CTA"}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"5."}]," Supporting proof (logos, stats, additional testimonials)"]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"6."}]," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-fg font-semibold","children":"Second CTA"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-xl border border-border bg-bg-muted p-4","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-widest text-fg-muted","children":"Long-form (VSL or sales pages)"}],["$","ol",null,{"className":"space-y-1 text-sm text-fg-muted","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"1."}]," Hero: problem-aware headline"]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"2."}]," Agitation: cost of the status quo"]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"3."}]," Proof block: 2–3 case snippets + stats"]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"4."}]," ",["$","span",null,{"className":"text-fg font-semibold","children":"First CTA"}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"5."}]," Mechanism + objection handling"]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-center gap-2","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"text-accent font-bold","children":"6."}]," Second proof block (longer testimonials, logos)"]}],"$L17"]}]]}]]}],"$L18"]}]
6:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"3 Implementations That Don't Require a Redesign"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-5 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"None of these require touching your ad creative, rebuilding the page, or waiting for a development sprint. Each is a bounded edit that can be tested without rebuilding the page."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-5","children":[["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"1. Insert a single stat above the hero CTA"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":["Take your strongest outcome number - a percentage lift, a revenue figure, a client count - and place it in a small badge or inline text directly above the primary button. One line is sufficient. The stat does not need a headline of its own. Example: ",["$","em",null,{"children":"\"See the issue, the evidence, and the next fix.\""}]," If you use an outcome or customer count instead, publish it only when the underlying record is current and inspectable."]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"2. Pull one testimonial into the hero section"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"Identify the shortest, most outcome-specific testimonial you have. Move it from the social proof section (wherever it currently lives) to directly beneath your subheadline. Keep it to two sentences maximum. Add the person's name, role, and company. This alone repositions the CTA from a cold ask to a reinforced recommendation."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"mb-1 text-lg font-semibold text-fg","children":"3. Add an outcome-anchored subheadline"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"If you have no testimonials ready to use, rewrite the subheadline to contain a verifiable result. Replace a generic benefit statement with a specific outcome claim only when you can substantiate it. A claim is not proof on its own; place the supporting method, source, and limitations close enough for the visitor to inspect."}]]}]]}]]}]
7:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-md border border-border bg-bg-panel p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-4 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"What to Use When You Have Zero Testimonials Yet"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-5 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"A new offer or a new landing page often has no reviews to show. That is not a reason to skip proof entirely - it is a reason to substitute a different, still verifiable, form of it until testimonials exist:"}],["$","ul",null,{"className":"space-y-4 text-fg-muted","children":[["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"A specific, verifiable process claim."}]," ","\"Every audit runs the same 9-signal diagnostic\" is proof of rigor even without an outcome number attached - it tells the visitor the evaluation is systematic, not improvised."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Founder or operator credibility, stated plainly."}]," ","A short, honest line about who is behind the offer and why - not a fabricated client count - can substitute for social proof when none exists yet."]}]]}],["$","li",null,{"className":"flex items-start gap-3","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"mt-2 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"}],["$","div",null,{"children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"font-semibold text-fg","children":"Transparent scarcity."}]," ","Stating plainly that you do not yet have a case study - and explaining what one would require to publish - reads as more trustworthy than an invented number, because it is falsifiable and specific."]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mt-5 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"What does not work: leaving the proof slot empty, or filling it with an unverifiable claim. Both cost more trust than an honest \"here is what we can show you right now\" statement."}]]}]
8:["$","section",null,{"className":"mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-accent/30 bg-accent/5 p-8","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"mb-3 text-2xl font-bold text-fg","children":"Find the proof leak on your page"}],["$","p",null,{"className":"mb-6 leading-relaxed text-fg-muted","children":"The free Nebula audit reports where the page may lose credibility before the CTA - missing proof, weak proof, misplaced proof. If the audit flags a proof leak, the $97 One-Leak Repair Sprint delivers a tailored kit for that high-confidence finding. You or your developer implements it, and the 30-day re-audit verifies the page condition."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex flex-wrap gap-4","children":[["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/audit?utm_source=learning-centre&utm_medium=organic-content","className":"inline-flex rounded bg-accent px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-bg hover:opacity-85 hover:bg-accent transition-colors","children":"Run the free audit"}],["$","$L2",null,{"href":"/learning-centre/paid-traffic-leak-map","className":"inline-flex rounded border border-accent px-6 py-3 font-semibold text-accent hover:bg-accent/10 transition-colors","children":"Open the leak map"}]]}]]}]
